# Agent C (adversarial): go-git#2384, range 2b34ce5d..b44afee6 (20 commits)

## Overall risk: low

The range is purely additive. `dotgit.go` has 503 lines added and 10 removed, and all 10 removed lines are the `Module` doc comment. The test files only add lines. No existing check is loosened, moved or removed. `Module` keeps `ValidStorageName`, the Windows Win32 check and the cleaned-prefix escape check from the base. It then adds a depth cap of 255 components and the nesting walk, and both only add refusals.

Every resolution error on a redirected (`commondir`) path fails closed, and absolute commondirs must stay inside a filesystem root. A relative `..` cannot leave the root or undo a symlink. Both reads are bounded: HEAD at 255 bytes and commondir at 1 MiB. Named pipes are refused before they are opened.

Hygiene is clean:
- no dependency, go.mod, CI, `go:generate` or `init()` changes;
- the only build tag is `//go:build unix` on a test file;
- no bidi or zero-width characters, and no non-ASCII added text;
- the one long hex string is an obvious fake SHA-256 HEAD in a test;
- the tests use only `TempDir` and memfs, and the fuzzers touch no network or home directory.

All 20 commits are authored and committed by Hidde Beydals with Signed-off-by. The messages contain no text aimed at reviewers or AI tools.

